# SPA fallback for Netlify and Cloudflare Pages.
#
# Prerendered routes (see scripts/prerender.mjs) are real files and are served
# directly — this rule only catches what has no file: /search, a mistyped URL, a
# slug that left the content set. 200 rather than 302 so the URL the visitor
# typed is the URL the router sees.
#
# Other hosts: Vercel uses vercel.json rewrites, Firebase uses firebase.json,
# nginx uses `try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html`, and GitHub Pages falls back to
# the dist/404.html the prerender writes. Any one of them is enough.
/*  /index.html  200
